  "body": "Fixes #632.\n\n## Problem\n\n`fetch` reads the method from the init object when it is set and otherwise from a `Request` input. Three guards in `$fetchRaw` consulted `options.method` only, so a prebuilt `Request` with a write method was treated as a `GET`:\n\n```ts\nconst ofetch = createFetch({\n  fetch: async () => { calls++; return new Response(\"unavailable\", { status: 503 }) },\n});\nawait ofetch(new Request(\"https://example.test/\", { method: \"POST\" })).catch(() => {});\n// calls === 2, but POST is documented as not retried by default\n```\n\nThree separate symptoms:\n\n1. **Retry** — `POST`/`PUT`/`PATCH`/`DELETE` passed as a `Request` got the `GET` policy of one retry, so a non-idempotent request was replayed.\n2. **Body serialization** — an overriding object body on a `Request` POST skipped `JSON.stringify` and the automatic `content-type: application/json`, so the raw object reached `fetch`.\n3. **HEAD** — a HEAD passed as a `Request` had its response body parsed, which is observable with a custom `fetch` that returns one.\n\n## Change\n\nAdds `resolveMethod(request, options)` to `src/utils.ts` — `options.method` first, then `(request as Request).method`, then `GET`, upper-cased — and uses it in all three places. The resolution happens after the `onRequest` hooks so a hook that swaps the request or sets a method is honoured.\n\nExplicit controls are deliberately untouched: a numeric `retry` and an explicit `options.method` both still take precedence over the `Request`.\n\n## Tests\n\nSix cases added to `test/index.test.ts`: the four write methods, HEAD parsing, and JSON body serialization cover the defect; a GET `Request`, an explicit `retry: 2`, and an explicit `method` override guard the behaviour that must not change.\n\nThe three defect tests fail on `main` with the source change reverted and pass with it. `vitest run` is 34/34, `eslint`, `prettier -c` and `tsc --noEmit` are clean.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved handling of prebuilt requests so HTTP methods are detected consistently.\n  * Retry behavior now correctly reflects the request method.\n  * Request bodies are serialized and response bodies are handled correctly for POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, GET, and HEAD requests.\n  * Explicit method and retry settings continue to take precedence when provided.\n  * Improved support for URL-encoded form bodies, including content types with parameters or mixed capitalization.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
